note: generics — one definition, every type. `any name` is a type variable;
note: the call decides what it stands for, and one concrete copy is compiled
note: for each type actually used.

a book has title as text, year as number

to head_or with xs as list of any item, fallback as any item giving any item:
    give back (maybe item 1 of xs) otherwise fallback

to kept with xs as list of any item, keep as (function taking any item giving yesno) giving list of any item:
    let out be an empty list of any item
    for each x in xs:
        if (keep with x):
            add x to out
    give back out

to mapped with xs as list of any input, change as (function taking any input giving any output) giving list of any output:
    let out be an empty list of any output
    for each x in xs:
        add (change with x) to out
    give back out

to is_recent with b as book giving yesno:
    give back b's year is at least 2000

to title_of with b as book giving text:
    give back "{b's title} ({b's year})"

to is_long with word as text giving yesno:
    give back length of word is more than 3

let library be a list of (a book with title "Dune", year 1965)
add (a book with title "Piranesi", year 2020) to library
add (a book with title "Klara", year 2021) to library

say (mapped with (kept with library, the function is_recent), the function title_of) joined with "; "

note: the same three helpers, now over plain text
let words be a list of "a", "tree", "of", "nights"
say (kept with words, the function is_long) joined with ", "
say (head_or with words, "none")
say (head_or with (an empty list of text), "none")
